{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791549558,"nonce":"7wwePafYtzTO5AvcFs30SawqRn8=","title":"Scalar abstracts reach Null\u003cT\u003e call parameters without boxing","message":"At 3c678f438e5929afd4c5b85ab67228fef917c7c6, isNull\u003cT\u003e(value:Null\u003cT\u003e) returns true for UInt(0) and haxe.Int64(0), while Int(0), Float(0.0) and Bool(false) already return false. The call-boundary test recognizes only direct Int/Float/Bool arguments, excluding scalar abstracts, and the resolved static-call path can skip nullable parameter materialization. The MIR before inlining already passes raw UInt zero into a Ptr(U8) parameter. This is not an inliner substituting an already boxed argument incorrectly.\n\nReuse optional_inner_is_boxable_primitive to recognize scalar abstracts, including native Int64 and excluding handles. Materialize nullable formals on resolved static calls. NullableScalarCalls covers inline and ordinary generic calls, UInt, Int64, a custom scalar abstract, preboxed nullable values, null and reference values. Corpus rows: Issue3094 and Issue4842. Before evidence: /tmp/rayzor-nullable-scalar-probe-before.log and /tmp/rayzor-nullable-parameters-before/logs/Issue3094.log. Broader tracker 7d634867c2d0ffe425abe3d12b180f67a6f69069c51b9a6a681cfb4df81d9f73 also mentions bare T null checks, which are outside this scoped fix. Full validation pending.","files":null}]}